{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1102005-can-do-devil-tigers-engage-in-noble-causes-or-good-deeds","id":1102005,"title":"Can/do Devil Tigers engage in noble causes or good deeds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-09T09:07:47-07:00","id":1102005,"title":"Can/do Devil Tigers engage in noble causes or good deeds?","content":"It's been a long while since I read any Kuei-Jin material so I am rusty. Do Devil Tigers ever try to improve the world or do they simply focus on punishing sinners? Perhaps they seal away banes in Inauspicious Objects to keep people safe from them? I have a desire to do a Dreamquest in the umbra that will have corresponding effects in the real world to make things better and to improve even the character of the people in the city the game is focused on and am curious if a Devil Tiger would ever bother with something like this. I understand they are trying to improve our world's over all spiritual health, but am unsure how married they are to their methods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 06-09-2017, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T09:16:16-07:00","id":1102008,"title":"","content":"Well if you pull the weeds of the garden isn't the garden over all a better place? They are noble with out being obnoxious about it like a Crane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T11:58:50-07:00","id":1102061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1102005-can-do-devil-tigers-engage-in-noble-causes-or-good-deeds?p=1102008#post1102008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if you pull the weeds of the garden isn't the garden over all a better place? They are noble with out being obnoxious about it like a Crane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking more about conventional heroics where the goal is less about the destruction and more about healing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T12:05:42-07:00","id":1102064,"title":"","content":"Healing is for soft hearted suckers, you tear out the cancer and let them deal with the aftermath. The scar serves as a reminder to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T13:47:27-07:00","id":1102096,"title":"","content":"Devil tigers are part of Wus and courts so even if they might not actually do it for &quot;enlightenment's&quot; sake they have all sorts of political reasons to act. They are also not robots of alien morality unable to have wants and desires outside becoming the most enlightened Devil Tiger ever. Look at Mr. Meng he likes chocolate. Generally DTs are more about punishing the wicked than saving the innocent but occasionally mixing it up can give them all sorts of insights. <br /> <br /> Suffice to say its complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T14:28:37-07:00","id":1102111,"title":"","content":"Well, if one were to torment and rather harshly reeducate a man who has been making all those he comes in contact with miserable and unhappy with his unrighteous behavior, then it would make all those lives he touches upon better as he becomes more moral and righteous in his day to day behavior. <br /> <br /> See also Charles Dickens's &quot;A Christmas Carol&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T15:00:52-07:00","id":1102119,"title":"","content":"A DT character in one of my games adopted and took care of the prostitutes in her city, eventually running prostitution in her city. Anytime that someone would abuse the prostitues, she would hunt them down and punish their wickedness (with the punishment proportional to the abuse). When a man killed a prostitue, she spent a week skinning him before packing him in salt and burying him alive. That is just an example of how a DT can do good (defending the weak) while pursuing her Dharma (punishing the wicked) and making a buck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:09:22-07:00","id":1102136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1102005-can-do-devil-tigers-engage-in-noble-causes-or-good-deeds?p=1102119#post1102119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A DT character in one of my games adopted and took care of the prostitutes in her city, eventually running prostitution in her city. Anytime that someone would abuse the prostitues, she would hunt them down and punish their wickedness (with the punishment proportional to the abuse). When a man killed a prostitue, she spent a week skinning him before packing him in salt and burying him alive. That is just an example of how a DT can do good (defending the weak) while pursuing her Dharma (punishing the wicked) and making a buck.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd actually get her censured fairly quickly. As opposed to cursing perpetrators to suffer from STIs or inciting angered spouses or lovers into murdering them. The key thing is that you have to make it look like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UVznerpOkTI\" target=\"_blank\">the natural consequences of failing to heed all safety warnings.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T16:25:19-07:00","id":1102142,"title":"","content":"Torturing and killing unrighteous people in the pursuit of their duties is an accepted part of being a DT (Devil Tiger, p. 24-25).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T21:38:17-07:00","id":1102188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1102005-can-do-devil-tigers-engage-in-noble-causes-or-good-deeds?p=1102142#post1102142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Torturing and killing unrighteous people in the pursuit of their duties is an accepted part of being a DT (Devil Tiger, p. 24-25).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if you do it in public or leave your results where they can be found. This is why there's an entire sect that's proscribed; they don't bother with subtlety, go in as monsters that cruelly kill people, and have prices on their heads for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T22:03:24-07:00","id":1102192,"title":"","content":"Who said anything about doing it in public or leaving it where anyone will find it? That sort of punishment is a private matter between the truly wicked and the DT who is purging their sins through their suffering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T22:45:17-07:00","id":1102201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1102005-can-do-devil-tigers-engage-in-noble-causes-or-good-deeds?p=1102136#post1102136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd actually get her censured fairly quickly. As opposed to cursing perpetrators to suffer from STIs or inciting angered spouses or lovers into murdering them. The key thing is that you have to make it look like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UVznerpOkTI\" target=\"_blank\">the natural consequences of failing to heed all safety warnings.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a lesson the Dharma teaches... eventually. Its not unknown for the young to dwell upon such things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T23:22:27-07:00","id":1102205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1102005-can-do-devil-tigers-engage-in-noble-causes-or-good-deeds?p=1102201#post1102201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's a lesson the Dharma teaches... eventually. Its not unknown for the young to dwell upon such things.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem to teach it so much as the elders have internalized how they picked up the devil and expect that the young will too, eventually. Kind of like the people who become cenobites in Hellraiser, they commit atrocities until it all seems pointless and they realize how banal it is. But they usually don't cool it completely on the atrocities, all the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T23:31:50-07:00","id":1102206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1102005-can-do-devil-tigers-engage-in-noble-causes-or-good-deeds?p=1102205#post1102205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't seem to teach it so much as the elders have internalized how they picked up the devil and expect that the young will too, eventually. Kind of like the people who become cenobites in Hellraiser, they commit atrocities until it all seems pointless and they realize how banal it is. But they usually don't cool it completely on the atrocities, all the same.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thus its not really unexpected for DTs in the pc range and even the occasional NPC to skin a sinner like above..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T06:32:06-07:00","id":1102249,"title":"","content":"The wicked need to be punished and giving someone who murders a vulnerable woman an STD or corrupting an innocent into murdering them is either a) laughably inadequate or b) against the teachings of the DT. The truly wicked deserve to suffer before they die in order to reduce their karmic debt. Skinning them alive over the course of a week and packing them in salt before burying them alive is not an atrocity (at least not according to the DT), it is an act of mercy because they may avoid going to the One Thousand Hells if they suffer enough in that one week to balance out the sins that they committed during their life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T08:11:37-07:00","id":1102272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1102005-can-do-devil-tigers-engage-in-noble-causes-or-good-deeds?p=1102249#post1102249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wicked need to be punished and giving someone who murders a vulnerable woman an STD or corrupting an innocent into murdering them</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said anything about corrupting an innocent? You cheat, you reap the rewards of breaking someone's innocence yourself. In this case, the possibility that they'll stab you for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is either a) laughably inadequate </div> </div> </div>It depends on which infection it is, isn't it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or b) against the teachings of the DT. The truly wicked deserve to suffer before they die in order to reduce their karmic debt. Skinning them alive over the course of a week and packing them in salt before burying them alive is not an atrocity (at least not according to the DT), it is an act of mercy because they may avoid going to the One Thousand Hells if they suffer enough in that one week to balance out the sins that they committed during their life. </div> </div> </div>Except that's not how it works, and Devil-Tigers should know it, because huge amounts of suffering in one week can just catapult you there on its own weight. A bunch of them probably got tortured to death before they died; obviously, it didn't function to keep them out of hell.<br /> <br /> In fact, they do know it, because they're not seeking to save people from hell. They'll be replacing the Yama Kings; they're going to preside over hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 06-10-2017, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T11:14:06-07:00","id":1102304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1102005-can-do-devil-tigers-engage-in-noble-causes-or-good-deeds?p=1102272#post1102272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Except that's not how it works, and Devil-Tigers should know it, because huge amounts of suffering in one week can just catapult you there on its own weight. A bunch of them probably got tortured to death before they died; obviously, it didn't function to keep them out of hell.<br /> <br /> In fact, they do know it, because they're not seeking to save people from hell. They'll be replacing the Yama Kings; they're going to preside over hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally those who feel that they were unjustly taken to hell rarely become Devil Tigers, so they don't really know it on a personal level. They may understand it on a pragmatic level but the number of &quot;completely innocent KJ who happened to have a really horrible death that you can totally prove this is the only reason they went to hell&quot; is not going to be the majority. Yes Objectively we know this the case OOCly but its a hard thing to prove in setting. Especially when there actively are people who end up in Hell who shouldn't be there at all. There's always been accidental arrivals.<br /> <br /> Every Dharma has a variety of sects for a reason, there's a reason there's a whole sect dedicated for the powerful some level of orthadoxy in the Dharma and a number of censured sects in spite of this. The character could totally believe and argue her point and from her perspective not be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}